The first full run passed G1–G7 and every attack, but correctly caught a flaw in my canonical key: a color permutation can reverse the row/column orientation of a bipartite block. I’m fixing that invariant. I’m also strengthening the shipping preset from \(k=22,s=48\) to \(k=24,s=56\); at the stronger setting, a one-million-node exact forward-checking solver still fails on all eight audit seeds, while the intended 276 pair checks stay under G9’s 300-operation cap.
